{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>This is the law of the Nazirite</b> – The meaning of the verse is: \"This is the law of the Nazirite who vows a Nazirite vow; his offering to HaShem according to his Naziriteship shall be, besides what his hand attains,\" or: \"This is the law of the Nazirite, and this is the law of his offering to HaShem according to his Naziriteship.\" It is also possible that it says: this is the law of the Nazirite — that he vows his offering upon his Naziriteship, meaning that he does not specify anything regarding the offering but rather vows, \"I will bring an offering upon my Naziriteship,\" or he says simply, \"I am a Nazirite,\" for since he has vowed a Nazirite vow, he is obligated in the offering mentioned. Then it goes back and says, <b>besides what his hand attains</b> — that if he is wealthy he may increase his offering, and according to his vow that he vows regarding the offerings, whether he is wealthy or poor, so shall he do according to the law of his Naziriteship, to add but not to diminish. And this was mentioned to teach that if he was wealthy and wanted to increase his offerings, or if he vowed from the outset, \"I am a Nazirite and I will bring a thousand burnt-offerings and peace-offerings,\" he must bring them all on the day of completion, and he may not drink wine until he offers all of them, for all of it is the law of his Naziriteship. It is also possible [that the meaning of] \"besides what his hand attains\" is that he shall do according to his vow that he vows, and this was mentioned because it is the way of the wealthy to vow thus."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:04.765285235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}